# Firmware reliability

- Avoid unnecessary blocking on critical Modbus/uplink paths; consider watchdog needs.
- Handle Wi-Fi disconnect/reconnect and Modbus timeouts/retries predictably.
- Bound buffers/allocations; avoid leaks/fragmentation where practical.
- Prevent malformed payloads from corrupting state.
- Failed uplinks: deliberate retry/backoff; preserve important telemetry across temporary loss where supported.
- Diagnostics useful without log floods. Do not silently lose data or make recovery hard.
